{%- comment -%}
CHANGE — IMPACTS / PRESSURES / IMPACT x PRESSURE — inline accordion.

Same shell and interaction pattern as _includes/env-des-accordion.liquid:
one panel open at a time, deep-linking via URL hash
(e.g. /themes/change/#pressures auto-expands Pressures and scrolls to it).

Impacts and Pressures panels use a nested accordion for the five
change categories — Agriculture, Vegetation, Bare Natural Surfaces,
Human-Made, Water, Ice & Snow, matching the EarthTrack app's change
taxonomy (assets/function/filter-map.js, changeInverted) — styled
like the top-level Impacts/Pressures/Impact x Pressure headers
(photo icon, title, count, chevron) but one level deeper, under the
env-des-subaccordion-* classes so they don't collide with the
top-level .env-des-accordion-item selectors in the script below. Each
category opens into a plain two-column A-Z list (env-desc-list / env-desc-row):
title + an (i) button per row, the (i) popping a fixed-position
tooltip with the item's image and description
(_includes/country-pipeline.liquid uses the same popover pattern).
No data restructuring needed for category membership: every item's
existing `image` field (a heading image like vegheader.png,
cropheader2.png, urbanheader.png, bareheader1.png, waterheader1/2.png,
snowheader.png) already encodes which of the five categories it
belongs to, so membership is derived in-template via `contains`
rather than stored on the item. All 220 items (77 impacts + 143
pressures) matched one of the five when checked — if a future item's
image doesn't match any, it silently won't appear under any category,
so keep new entries on the existing filenames or extend
change_categories below.
  _data/themes/change/impacts/index.yml   (title, image, content)
  _data/themes/change/pressures/index.yml (title, image, content)

Impacts additionally look up their related pressures — press the
"Pressures" button next to an impact's (i) to reveal a chip list of the pressures that can cause
it (click a chip to show that pressure's definition). The mapping is:
  _data/themes/change/impact-pressure-links.yml (impact title -> [pressure titles])
built from the Global Change Taxonomy's supporting-information dataset
(Lucas et al. 2022, Global Change Biology, DOI 10.1111/gcb.16346;
data: github.com/livingearth-system/Globalchangeframework,
Impacts-(pressures).md), reconciled against this site's own impact and
pressure titles (a handful of spelling variants — e.g. "understory"
vs. this site's "understorey", "fertiliser" vs. "fertilizer" — were
matched by hand; see the mapping-generation notes kept outside this
repo). It covers 73 of the 77 impacts (236 links total); the 4
uncovered impacts (INVASIVE OR EXOTIC SPECIES, MINE CONSTRUCTION,
WATER MOVEMENT CHANGE, WAVE ACTION) aren't listed as an "impact
(pressure)" pair anywhere in the source table, so they render as
plain non-interactive rows with no chip panel.

The Impact x Pressure panel reuses the Publications page's
country-filter-pill pattern (_includes/publications.liquid). It loops
over the existing per-country data files and tags each card with its
country in-template, so none of that data needs merging either:
  _data/themes/change/ip/global/index.yml
  _data/themes/change/ip/wales/index.yml
  _data/themes/change/ip/australia/index.yml

Switzerland and Papua New Guinea don't have case-study data yet (both
still "#" placeholders in _data/themes/change/ip/index.yml) — add
"switzerland|Switzerland" / "png|Papua New Guinea" to ip_countries
below once real _data/themes/change/ip/<country>/index.yml files exist
for them.

Usage: {% include change-accordion.liquid %}
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="env-des-accordion change-impacts-only" id="change-accordion">
  {%- comment -%}
  IMPACTS ONLY (for now): the Impacts panel is open by default and its "Impacts"
  header is hidden by the change-impacts-only class. To bring Pressures and
  Impact x Pressure Examples back: delete change-impacts-only from the div above,
  delete the word "open" from the Impacts item, and remove the comment tags
  around the two hidden blocks further down (search for "HIDDEN FOR NOW").
  {%- endcomment -%}

  <!-- Shared category taxonomy for Impacts and Pressures:
       id|Label|image-substring-to-match|icon-image  (Water also separately matches "snow") -->
  {% assign change_categories = "agriculture|Agriculture|crop|/assets/img/wales/crop-type.jpg;vegetation|Vegetation|veg|/assets/img/wales/vegetation.jpg;bare|Bare Natural Surfaces|bare|/assets/img/wales/dem.jpg;human-made|Human-Made|urban|/assets/img/wales/artificial-materials.jpg;water|Water, Ice & Snow|water|/assets/img/wales/water.jpg" | split: ";" %}

  <!-- IMPACTS -->
  {% assign all_pressures = site.data['themes']['change']['pressures'].index %}
  {% assign impacts = site.data['themes']['change']['impacts'].index %}
  <div class="env-des-accordion-item open" data-cat="impacts">
    <button type="button" class="env-des-accordion-header" data-target="impacts">
      <span class="env-des-accordion-title">Impacts</span>
      <span class="env-des-accordion-count">{{ impacts | size }}</span>
      <svg class="env-des-accordion-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M12.53 16.28a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06 0l-7.5-7.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06-1.06L12 14.69l6.97-6.97a.75.75 0 1 1 1.06 1.06l-7.5 7.5Z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
    </button>
    <div class="env-des-accordion-panel" id="impacts">
      <div class="env-des-accordion-panel-inner">
        <div class="env-des-subaccordion">
          {% for cat in change_categories %}
          {% assign parts = cat | split: "|" %}
          {% assign cat_key = parts[0] %}
          {% assign cat_label = parts[1] %}
          {% assign cat_match = parts[2] %}
          {% assign cat_image = parts[3] %}
          {% assign cat_count = 0 %}
          {% for item in impacts %}
            {% unless item.title == blank %}
            {% assign m = false %}
            {% if item.image contains cat_match %}{% assign m = true %}{% endif %}
            {% if cat_key == "water" and item.image contains "snow" %}{% assign m = true %}{% endif %}
            {% if m %}{% assign cat_count = cat_count | plus: 1 %}{% endif %}
            {% endunless %}
          {% endfor %}
          <div class="env-des-subaccordion-item" data-subcat="impacts-{{ cat_key }}">
            <button type="button" class="env-des-subaccordion-header" data-subtarget="impacts-{{ cat_key }}">
              <img src="{{ cat_image | relative_url }}" alt="" class="env-des-subaccordion-icon">
              <span class="env-des-subaccordion-title">{{ cat_label }}</span>
              <span class="env-des-subaccordion-count">{{ cat_count }}</span>
              <svg class="env-des-subaccordion-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M12.53 16.28a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06 0l-7.5-7.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06-1.06L12 14.69l6.97-6.97a.75.75 0 1 1 1.06 1.06l-7.5 7.5Z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
            </button>
            <div class="env-des-subaccordion-panel" id="impacts-{{ cat_key }}">
              <div class="env-des-subaccordion-panel-inner">
                {%- comment -%} One A-Z table per category: impact (+ info icon) on the left, all the pressures that can cause it on the right. {%- endcomment -%}
                {% assign list_items = impacts | sort_natural: "title" %}
                <table class="change-table">
                  <thead>
                    <tr>
                      <th scope="col">Impact</th>
                      <th scope="col">Pressures that can cause it <span class="change-table-hint">(click to show)</span></th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
                  {% for item in list_items %}
                  {% unless item.title == blank %}
                  {% assign is_match = false %}
                  {% if item.image contains cat_match %}{% assign is_match = true %}{% endif %}
                  {% if cat_key == "water" and item.image contains "snow" %}{% assign is_match = true %}{% endif %}
                  {% if is_match %}
                  {% assign display_title = item.title | strip | downcase | capitalize %}
                  {% assign related_pressures = site.data['themes']['change']['impact-pressure-links'][item.title] %}
                  <tr>
                    <th scope="row" class="change-table-impact">
                      <div class="change-table-impact-inner">
                        <span class="env-desc-item-title">{{ display_title }}</span>
                        {% if item.content %}
                        <button type="button" class="env-desc-item-info" aria-label="What is {{ display_title }}?">i</button>
                        <span class="env-desc-item-tooltip env-desc-item-tooltip-media">
                          {% if item.image %}<img src="{% if item.image contains 'http' %}{{ item.image }}{% else %}{{ item.image | relative_url }}{% endif %}" alt="" class="env-desc-item-tooltip-img">{% endif %}
                          <span class="env-desc-item-tooltip-text">{{ item.content }}</span>
                        </span>
                        {% endif %}
                      </div>
                    </th>
                    <td class="change-table-pressures change-pressure-cell">
                      {% if related_pressures %}
                      <button type="button" class="env-desc-pressures-btn" aria-expanded="false">Pressures ({{ related_pressures | size }})<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M12.53 16.28a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06 0l-7.5-7.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06-1.06L12 14.69l6.97-6.97a.75.75 0 1 1 1.06 1.06l-7.5 7.5Z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg></button>
                      <div class="change-pressure-reveal" hidden>
                        <div class="env-desc-pressure-chips">
                          {% for pr in related_pressures %}
                          {% assign pr_def = all_pressures | where: "title", pr | first %}
                          {% if pr_def.content %}
                          <button type="button" class="env-desc-pressure-chip" data-pressure="{{ pr | slugify }}" aria-expanded="false">{{ pr | strip | downcase | capitalize }}</button>
                          {% else %}
                          <span class="env-desc-pressure-chip is-static">{{ pr | strip | downcase | capitalize }}</span>
                          {% endif %}
                          {% endfor %}
                        </div>
                        <div class="env-desc-pressure-defs">
                          {% for pr in related_pressures %}
                          {% assign pr_def = all_pressures | where: "title", pr | first %}
                          {% if pr_def.content %}
                          <div class="env-desc-pressure-def" data-pressure-def="{{ pr | slugify }}" hidden>
                            <strong>{{ pr | strip | downcase | capitalize }}</strong> &mdash; {{ pr_def.content }}
                          </div>
                          {% endif %}
                          {% endfor %}
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      {% else %}
                      <span class="change-table-none">&mdash;</span>
                      {% endif %}
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  {% endif %}
                  {% endunless %}
                  {% endfor %}
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
  HIDDEN FOR NOW: Pressures and Impact x Pressure Examples. See the note at the top of this div.

  <!-- PRESSURES -->
  {% assign pressures = site.data['themes']['change']['pressures'].index %}
  <div class="env-des-accordion-item" data-cat="pressures">
    <button type="button" class="env-des-accordion-header" data-target="pressures">
      <span class="env-des-accordion-title">Pressures</span>
      <span class="env-des-accordion-count">{{ pressures | size }}</span>
      <svg class="env-des-accordion-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M12.53 16.28a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06 0l-7.5-7.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06-1.06L12 14.69l6.97-6.97a.75.75 0 1 1 1.06 1.06l-7.5 7.5Z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
    </button>
    <div class="env-des-accordion-panel" id="pressures">
      <div class="env-des-accordion-panel-inner">
        <div class="env-des-subaccordion">
          {% for cat in change_categories %}
          {% assign parts = cat | split: "|" %}
          {% assign cat_key = parts[0] %}
          {% assign cat_label = parts[1] %}
          {% assign cat_match = parts[2] %}
          {% assign cat_image = parts[3] %}
          {% assign cat_count = 0 %}
          {% for item in pressures %}
            {% unless item.title == blank %}
            {% assign m = false %}
            {% if item.image contains cat_match %}{% assign m = true %}{% endif %}
            {% if cat_key == "water" and item.image contains "snow" %}{% assign m = true %}{% endif %}
            {% if m %}{% assign cat_count = cat_count | plus: 1 %}{% endif %}
            {% endunless %}
          {% endfor %}
          <div class="env-des-subaccordion-item" data-subcat="pressures-{{ cat_key }}">
            <button type="button" class="env-des-subaccordion-header" data-subtarget="pressures-{{ cat_key }}">
              <img src="{{ cat_image | relative_url }}" alt="" class="env-des-subaccordion-icon">
              <span class="env-des-subaccordion-title">{{ cat_label }}</span>
              <span class="env-des-subaccordion-count">{{ cat_count }}</span>
              <svg class="env-des-subaccordion-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M12.53 16.28a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06 0l-7.5-7.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06-1.06L12 14.69l6.97-6.97a.75.75 0 1 1 1.06 1.06l-7.5 7.5Z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
            </button>
            <div class="env-des-subaccordion-panel" id="pressures-{{ cat_key }}">
              <div class="env-des-subaccordion-panel-inner">
                {% assign list_items = pressures | sort_natural: "title" %}
                {% assign half = cat_count | divided_by: 2.0 | ceil %}
                {% assign idx = 0 %}
                <div class="env-desc-list">
                  <div class="env-desc-list-col">
                  {% for item in list_items %}
                  {% unless item.title == blank %}
                  {% assign is_match = false %}
                  {% if item.image contains cat_match %}{% assign is_match = true %}{% endif %}
                  {% if cat_key == "water" and item.image contains "snow" %}{% assign is_match = true %}{% endif %}
                  {% if is_match %}
                  {% if idx == half %}</div><div class="env-desc-list-col">{% endif %}
                  {% assign idx = idx | plus: 1 %}
                  {% assign display_title = item.title | strip | downcase | capitalize %}
                  <div class="env-desc-row">
                    <span class="env-desc-item-title">{{ display_title }}</span>
                    {% if item.content %}
                    <button type="button" class="env-desc-item-info" aria-label="What is {{ display_title }}?">i</button>
                    <span class="env-desc-item-tooltip env-desc-item-tooltip-media">
                      {% if item.image %}<img src="{% if item.image contains 'http' %}{{ item.image }}{% else %}{{ item.image | relative_url }}{% endif %}" alt="" class="env-desc-item-tooltip-img">{% endif %}
                      <span class="env-desc-item-tooltip-text">{{ item.content }}</span>
                    </span>
                    {% endif %}
                  </div>
                  {% endif %}
                  {% endunless %}
                  {% endfor %}
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- IMPACT x PRESSURE EXAMPLES -->
  {% assign ip_countries = "global|Global,wales|Wales,australia|Australia" | split: "," %}
  <div class="env-des-accordion-item" data-cat="impact-pressure">
    <button type="button" class="env-des-accordion-header" data-target="impact-pressure">
      <span class="env-des-accordion-title">Impact &times; Pressure Examples</span>
      <svg class="env-des-accordion-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M12.53 16.28a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06 0l-7.5-7.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06-1.06L12 14.69l6.97-6.97a.75.75 0 1 1 1.06 1.06l-7.5 7.5Z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
    </button>
    <div class="env-des-accordion-panel" id="impact-pressure">
      <div class="env-des-accordion-panel-inner">

        <div class="pub-filters">
          <div class="pub-filter-group">
            <span class="pub-filter-label">Country</span>
            <div class="pub-filter-row" data-filter-type="country">
              <button class="pub-filter-pill is-active" type="button" data-filter-value="all">All</button>
              {% for src in ip_countries %}
                {% assign parts = src | split: "|" %}
                <button class="pub-filter-pill" type="button" data-filter-value="{{ parts[1] }}">{{ parts[1] }}</button>
              {% endfor %}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pub-empty" hidden>No examples match this filter.</div>

        <div class="pub-grid">
          {% for src in ip_countries %}
            {% assign parts = src | split: "|" %}
            {% assign key = parts[0] %}
            {% assign label = parts[1] %}
            {% assign country_items = site.data['themes']['change']['ip'][key].index %}
            {% for item in country_items %}
              {% unless item.title == blank %}
              <div class="pub-card" data-country="{{ label }}">
                <span class="pub-card-badge">{{ label }}</span>
                {% if item.url and item.url != "#" %}
                <a class="pub-card-title" href="{% if item.url contains 'http' %}{{ item.url }}{% else %}{{ item.url | relative_url }}{% endif %}">{{ item.title }}</a>
                {% else %}
                <span class="pub-card-title pub-card-title-nolink">{{ item.title }}</span>
                {% endif %}
                <div class="pub-card-authors">{{ item.content }}</div>
              </div>
              {% endunless %}
            {% endfor %}
          {% endfor %}
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {%- endcomment -%}

</div>

<script>
(function () {
  var root = document.getElementById('change-accordion');
  if (!root) { return; }
  var items = root.querySelectorAll('.env-des-accordion-item');

  function openItem(id) {
    items.forEach(function (item) {
      item.classList.toggle('open', item.getAttribute('data-cat') === id);
    });
  }

  items.forEach(function (item) {
    var header = item.querySelector('.env-des-accordion-header');
    header.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var id = item.getAttribute('data-cat');
      var alreadyOpen = item.classList.contains('open');
      items.forEach(function (i) { i.classList.remove('open'); });
      if (!alreadyOpen) {
        item.classList.add('open');
        history.replaceState(null, '', '#' + id);
        requestAnimationFrame(function () {
          header.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
        });
      } else {
        history.replaceState(null, '', '#change-accordion');
      }
    });
  });

  var hash = window.location.hash.replace('#', '');
  var validIds = Array.prototype.map.call(items, function (i) { return i.getAttribute('data-cat'); });
  if (hash && validIds.indexOf(hash) !== -1) {
    openItem(hash);
    var target = root.querySelector('.env-des-accordion-item[data-cat="' + hash + '"]');
    if (target) {
      setTimeout(function () { target.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' }); }, 100);
    }
  }

  // Nested category accordions (Impacts / Pressures panels) — same
  // open/close pattern as the top-level accordion above, one level
  // deeper, scoped to each panel's own .env-des-subaccordion wrapper
  // so Impacts and Pressures don't affect each other.
  var subaccordions = root.querySelectorAll('.env-des-subaccordion');
  subaccordions.forEach(function (wrap) {
    var subItems = wrap.querySelectorAll('.env-des-subaccordion-item');
    subItems.forEach(function (subItem) {
      var subHeader = subItem.querySelector('.env-des-subaccordion-header');
      subHeader.addEventListener('click', function () {
        var alreadyOpen = subItem.classList.contains('open');
        subItems.forEach(function (i) { i.classList.remove('open'); });
        if (!alreadyOpen) { subItem.classList.add('open'); }
      });
    });
  });

  // Deep link to one category, e.g. /themes/change/#impacts-vegetation
  var catHash = window.location.hash.replace('#', '');
  subaccordions.forEach(function (wrap) {
    wrap.querySelectorAll('.env-des-subaccordion-item').forEach(function (subItem) {
      if (subItem.getAttribute('data-subcat') === catHash) {
        subItem.classList.add('open');
        setTimeout(function () { subItem.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' }); }, 100);
      }
    });
  });

  // Info-icon tooltips (Impacts / Pressures cards) — same fixed-position
  // popover behaviour as _includes/country-pipeline.liquid.
  var infoButtons = root.querySelectorAll('.env-desc-item-info');

  function closeTooltip(t) {
    t.classList.remove('is-open');
    if (t._homeParent) {
      t._homeParent.insertBefore(t, t._homeNext);
    }
    t.style.position = '';
    t.style.top = '';
    t.style.left = '';
    t.style.right = '';
    t.style.width = '';
    t.style.margin = '';
  }

  infoButtons.forEach(function (btn) {
    var tooltip = btn.nextElementSibling;
    tooltip._homeParent = tooltip.parentNode;
    tooltip._homeNext = tooltip.nextSibling;

    btn.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      e.preventDefault();
      e.stopPropagation();
      var wasOpen = tooltip.classList.contains('is-open');

      document.querySelectorAll('.env-desc-item-tooltip.is-open').forEach(closeTooltip);

      if (!wasOpen) {
        var btnRect = btn.getBoundingClientRect();

        tooltip.classList.add('measuring');
        var tooltipWidth = tooltip.offsetWidth;
        var tooltipHeight = tooltip.offsetHeight;
        tooltip.classList.remove('measuring');

        document.body.appendChild(tooltip);

        var top = btnRect.bottom + 6;
        if (top + tooltipHeight > window.innerHeight - 8) {
          top = btnRect.top - tooltipHeight - 6;
        }
        if (top < 8) { top = 8; }

        var left = btnRect.left;
        if (left + tooltipWidth > window.innerWidth - 8) {
          left = window.innerWidth - tooltipWidth - 8;
        }
        if (left < 8) { left = 8; }

        tooltip.style.position = 'fixed';
        tooltip.style.top = top + 'px';
        tooltip.style.left = left + 'px';
        tooltip.style.right = 'auto';
        tooltip.style.width = tooltipWidth + 'px';
        tooltip.style.margin = '0';
        tooltip.classList.add('is-open');
      }
    });
  });

  document.addEventListener('click', function () {
    document.querySelectorAll('.env-desc-item-tooltip.is-open').forEach(closeTooltip);
  });
  window.addEventListener('scroll', function () {
    document.querySelectorAll('.env-desc-item-tooltip.is-open').forEach(closeTooltip);
  }, { passive: true });

  // "Pressures (n)" button in the table: show / hide that impact's pressures.
  root.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
    var btn = e.target.closest('.env-desc-pressures-btn');
    if (!btn) { return; }
    var cell = btn.closest('.change-pressure-cell');
    var reveal = cell && cell.querySelector('.change-pressure-reveal');
    if (!reveal) { return; }
    reveal.hidden = !reveal.hidden;
    btn.classList.toggle('is-open', !reveal.hidden);
    btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', reveal.hidden ? 'false' : 'true');
  });

  // Pressure chips: clicking a chip shows/hides that pressure's
  // definition (from _data/themes/change/pressures/index.yml) under the
  // chips in the same table cell. Several can be open at once. Chips with no matching
  // definition render as static <span>s and are ignored here.
  root.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
    var chip = e.target.closest('button.env-desc-pressure-chip');
    if (!chip) { return; }
    var cell = chip.closest('.change-pressure-cell');
    if (!cell) { return; }
    var def = cell.querySelector('.env-desc-pressure-def[data-pressure-def="' + chip.getAttribute('data-pressure') + '"]');
    var open = chip.classList.toggle('is-selected');
    chip.setAttribute('aria-expanded', open ? 'true' : 'false');
    if (def) { def.hidden = !open; }
  });

  // Country filter pills (Impact x Pressure panel only)
  var pubCards = root.querySelectorAll('.pub-card');
  var pubEmpty = root.querySelector('.pub-empty');
  var pubRow = root.querySelector('.pub-filter-row[data-filter-type="country"]');
  if (pubRow) {
    var active = 'all';
    function applyFilter() {
      var visibleCount = 0;
      pubCards.forEach(function (card) {
        var show = active === 'all' || card.getAttribute('data-country') === active;
        card.hidden = !show;
        if (show) { visibleCount++; }
      });
      pubEmpty.hidden = visibleCount !== 0;
    }
    pubRow.querySelectorAll('.pub-filter-pill').forEach(function (btn) {
      btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
        pubRow.querySelectorAll('.pub-filter-pill').forEach(function (b) { b.classList.remove('is-active'); });
        btn.classList.add('is-active');
        active = btn.getAttribute('data-filter-value');
        applyFilter();
      });
    });
  }
})();
</script>